 "source": "Topps checklist PDF (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0662/9749/5709/files/2026_Bowman_Chrome_Baseball_Sapphire_Edition_Checklist.pdf?v=1790956155, read 2026-10-08) + Checklist Insider (https://www.checklistinsider.com/2026-bowman-chrome-sapphire-baseball, read 2026-10-06/08) + Topps product page (https://www.topps.com/pages/bowman-chrome-sapphire: 'Available October 7 at 12pm ET on EQL', every box at least one autograph and three colored parallels)",
 "status": "published",
 "note": "R8: this is the October online-exclusive Sapphire edition of SEPTEMBER's 2026 Bowman Chrome — not June's 2026 Bowman Sapphire Edition (May Bowman in sapphire, BSPA autos; data/sets/bowman-sapphire-2026.json). 200-card base (100 veterans/rookies + Chrome Prospects BCP-151 to BCP-250), 34 Chrome Sapphire Prospect Autographs (CSPA-), 11 Sapphire Selections Autographs. Hobby box $599.99, 8 packs x 4 cards, 1 autograph + 3 sapphire parallels per box (CI); case = 10 boxes (retailer case listings, MED). Auto pack odds (CI): CSPA 1:16; Green 1:32, Gold 1:63, Orange 1:125, Black 1:308, Red 1:618, Padparadscha 1:2,972 — print runs (CI, read Oct 8; base auto /199 and Green /99 also Slabsquatch/Baseballcardpedia): base /199, Green /99, Gold /50, Orange /25, Black /10, Red /5, Padparadscha 1/1 — KB 03 §9. Sapphire Selections Autographs (11: Eldridge, Benge, Bonemer, Quintero, Renteria, Griffin, Okamoto, L. Hernandez, Caissie, Yesavage, Asigen; 1:156 packs) are an insert program — never 1st-logo cards, not index material, so not listed as rows. The Topps checklist PDF (Oct 8) confirms a 34th prospect auto, 'BSPA-EHA Eric Hartman' (last line, June Sapphire's prefix). He has no September CPA; his 1st Bowman auto is May 2026 Bowman CPA-EHA (BB26/BOW26), so the row is not index material and is left out here; its card code and logo are unverified until a card surfaces (KB 02 §1, GAPS G24). Released Oct 7 2026 (Topps.com EQL); ship date not published.",
 "firstNote": "Sapphire is the sapphire parallel edition of September's 2026 Bowman Chrome (parallelOf): the same cards in sapphire, so each 1st logo mirrors that set's audited flag exactly (the June Sapphire precedent). 33 of the 34 CSPA players are September CPA 1sts and carry the flag here (`mirrors` = the September number). Sapphire Selections Autographs are an insert program and never carry the 1st logo. BCP sapphire rows mirror September's BCP flags. Neither the Topps PDF nor CI marks 1sts on this checklist; the mirrored flag is [MED] (rule + 2025 Chrome Sapphire CI marks) until a 2026 card image shows the logo (KB 02 §3d).",
 "firstRule": "Card carries the 1st logo iff it is the player’s first Bowman-family card of its kind (non-auto | auto). A parallel edition carries its parent card's logo. Rule set by Mo, Sep 9 2026.",
 "firstAudit": {
  "verified": "2026-10-06",
  "by": "chief-of-staff (Claude) — Mo in chat Oct 6 2026: 'track this as an index and the cards per our bowman rules'",
